Yesterday I finally managed to make a pacifist game.
It was a regular gnomish healer, and additional conducts were
weaponless and polyselfless. Dumplog is at
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/solidsnail/dumplog/1223570377.nh343.txt

Nothing much to say: I was scumming in the sense that I was doing the
protection racket and if there was not a magic lamp until minetown, I
usually started another game.
This game, not having found a magic lamp I was ready to quit when I
decided to take a go at the minetown fountains: got the wish and the
Archon came peacefull.

The /oWishing of the castle came at 0:2 and I wished for the Orb of
fate and the PYEC: with this combination I had infinite charges for my
orb and could detect poly and level teleport traps on every level and
disarm them.

With polyself I got enough !oGL for my archon to get to level 49, and
I also gave her +6 excalibur (got it at +3 from a bones), a "oLS and
some enchanted armor.

Next I'll try to make a pacifist+weaponless+foodless (+ maybe
polyselfless) monk with random alignment.

I'm a bit of an endurance player, so I would like to see how a real
pacifist is done. I've seen references to pacifist games where very
few monsters die, and sometimes even the quest nemesis is spared.
Could someone point me to some ttyrecs/posts of such ascentions,
please?

